1991 - Green project
james gosling and a small tean at sun microsystems explore software for consumer devices

1991 - Named "Oak"
The new language is named after an oak tree outside gosling's office 

1992 - Star7 demo
A handheld prototype (*7) shows oak code running on custom hardware 

1995 - Renamed java
"Oak" is already trademarked: java is publicly announced in may 1995

1996 - JDK1.0
First official released (january -1996) - java goes mainstream 
